    "result_text": "All 45 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The redesign is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and every value derived from it followed suit.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Rewrote `generateCustomerCode` to take the `Owner` and build `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n  - `REGION` comes from a new `deriveRegion(postcode, city)` helper \u2014 postcode range first (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), then the city-to-region table, else `UNKNOWN`.\n  - `HASH8` is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (telephone is already E.164-normalized at that point). The sequence-number logic is gone.\n- Added a shared `shortSha256Hex(input, length)` helper and refactored `generateHouseholdId` to reuse it.\n- Updated the call site and comments.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- `deriveLocality` now reads the region straight off the region-and-hash `customerCode` (the segment before the first hyphen), rather than recomputing from postcode/city \u2014 so locality moves onto the new identity.\n\nThe membership number (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), its Luhn check digit, and the create audit line all already derive from `customerCode`, so they automatically pick up the new region-and-hash value. Column widths (`customer_code VARCHAR(20)`, `membership_number VARCHAR(30)`) comfortably fit the new format (max 16 / 20 chars).\n\nAll 45 acceptance tests (including the identity-focused Cp09/14/16/17/21/30/31/32) pass.",
